#: qml/components/Tutorial.qml:101
msgid "Welcome to Modular Launcher"
msgstr ""

#: qml/components/Tutorial.qml:102
msgid ""
"Every screen of this launcher is a page you add and configure yourself. This "
"tour shows the parts of the Home page. You can leave it at any time and find "
"it again in the help."
msgstr ""

#: qml/components/Tutorial.qml:106
msgid "The search bar"
msgstr ""

#: qml/components/Tutorial.qml:107
msgid ""
"Type to filter the applications of this page. The same field finds your "
"contacts and calculates an expression. The icon on its right opens a web "
"search, with the engine chosen in the settings of this page."
msgstr ""

#: qml/components/Tutorial.qml:111
msgid "The widgets"
msgstr ""

#: qml/components/Tutorial.qml:112
msgid ""
"The clock, the weather, the alarms, the last calls, the last messages and "
"the events live here. Press and hold a widget to open its own settings, and "
"choose the ones to show in the settings of this page."
msgstr ""

#: qml/components/Tutorial.qml:116
msgid "The favorite applications"
msgstr ""

#: qml/components/Tutorial.qml:117
msgid ""
"The applications you choose stay at the top of this page, above the others. "
"Add, remove and reorder them in the settings of this page."
msgstr ""

#: qml/components/Tutorial.qml:121
msgid "The applications"
msgstr ""

#: qml/components/Tutorial.qml:122
msgid ""
"All the applications installed on the device, and the custom icons you "
"create. Touch one to launch it, press and hold it to uninstall it or to take "
"a custom icon off, and pull down to refresh the list."
msgstr ""

#: qml/components/Tutorial.qml:127
msgid "Moving between pages"
msgstr ""

#: qml/components/Tutorial.qml:128
msgid ""
"The bar at the bottom shows one icon per page of the launcher. Touch an icon "
"to jump to that page, or swipe left and right, on this bar or on the page "
"itself, to go from one page to the next."
msgstr ""

#: qml/components/Tutorial.qml:133
msgid "The configuration bar"
msgstr ""

#: qml/components/Tutorial.qml:134
msgid ""
"Swipe up from the bottom of the screen to open it: add a custom icon, manage "
"the pages, configure the launcher and its autostart, open the help and the "
"about page."
msgstr ""

#: qml/components/Tutorial.qml:138
msgid "Configuring the pages"
msgstr ""

#: qml/components/Tutorial.qml:139
msgid ""
"In that bar, Manage pages opens the list of your pages. The plus sign adds "
"one: another home, a clock, a calendar, photos, music, videos, news feeds, "
"tasks, folders or your Nextcloud files. Touching a page opens its own "
"settings. Enjoy your launcher."
msgstr ""

